window.DOCS["6ad70db349375d6d80094247"]={"id":"6ad70db349375d6d80094247","summary":{"title_zh":"溝通、教育與公眾意識","what":"這是一份由第一工作小組主席提出的會議室文件（CRP，決議草案），旨在推動生物多樣性教育的全球行動計畫草案，並鼓勵各方透過教育支持昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要的目標。","points":["建議使用「生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫」草案，並作為後續意見的基礎（「落實」一詞仍在方括號內）。","邀請原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人透過同儕審查提供意見，以完善該計畫。","（整段在方括號內）邀請各方與其他政府考慮提供充足、可預測且可取得的技術與財務支持，特別是開發中國家，包括低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家。","要求執行秘書在資源允許下，並與非正式諮詢委員會協商，透過資訊交換機制促進以聯合國六種正式語文提供的數位教育資源共享，同時尊重原住民族與地方社區的權利。","鼓勵締約方在國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，以及國家與次國家教育計畫中，納入生物多樣性教育。","鼓勵締約方建立或強化國家級機制或平台，協調各部會、教育機構與科學組織之間的生物多樣性溝通與教育工作。"],"open":["第 5 段（整段）：是否「鼓勵」締約方、「邀請」其他政府使用並落實該全球行動計畫，以支持綱要所需的轉型行動（整段仍在方括號內）。","第 7 段：「其他非國家政府的參與者」與「其他相關利害關係人」的定義與範圍。","第 7 段：是否提供專門且易於取得的資源給原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，以支持社區主導的教育倡議，並應符合國家立法與國家機制。","第 8(c) 段：是否將聯合國教科文組織綠色教育夥伴關係、生態系復育十年、氣候變遷框架下的氣候賦權行動及 PISA 氣候素養評估等納入合作範疇。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p001.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Distr.: Limited"},{"t":"20 October 2026"},{"t":"Original: English"},{"t":"Conference of the Parties to the"},{"t":"Convention on Biological Diversity"},{"t":"Seventeenth meeting"},{"t":"Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026"},{"t":"Agenda item 12 (c)"},{"t":"Matters relating to support mechanisms for the"},{"t":"implementation and awareness of the Convention"},{"t":"on Biological Diversity and the Kunming-Montreal"},{"t":"Global Biodiversity Framework: Communication,"},{"t":"education and public awareness"},{"t":"Working Group I"},{"t":"Communication, education and public awareness"},{"t":"Draft decision submitted by the Chair of Working Group I"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling its decision 16/10 of 1 November 2024,"},{"t":"1. Takes note of the progress report on the implementation of the suggested actions to align the programme of work on communication, education and public awareness for the Convention on Biological Diversity1 with the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,2 as provided in document CBD/SBI/7/13;"},{"t":"2. Welcomes the successful hosting by South Africa of the global celebration of the International Day for Biological Diversity in 2026 under the theme “Acting locally for global impact”;"},{"t":"3. Reiterates its request to the Executive Secretary in subparagraph 6 (c) of decision 16/10 to keep the topic of communication, education and public awareness under review at its eighteenth and nineteenth meetings;"},{"t":"4. Welcomes the draft global plan of action for education on biodiversity contained in the annex to the present decision, and recommends its use, including as a basis for further inputs, noting that it is a living document that will be further developed;"},{"t":"[5. Encourages Parties, and invites other Governments, [to use] [and implement] the draft global plan of action for education on biodiversity, with a view to supporting the transformative actions needed to achieve the goals and targets of the Framework and its vision of a world living in harmony with nature;]"},{"t":"6. Invites Parties, other Governments, relevant organizations, indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and other stakeholders to provide inputs, through a peer-review process, to further develop the global plan of action;"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 Decision 15/4, annex."}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6\n分發：限閱\n2026年10月20日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6<br />\n分發：限閱<br />\n2026年10月20日<br />\n原文：英文</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 12 (c)\n關於落實生物多樣性公約與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之支援機制及提升意識之事項：溝通、教育與大眾意識","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 12 (c)<br />\n關於落實生物多樣性公約與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之支援機制及提升意識之事項：溝通、教育與大眾意識</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"第一工作小組","html":"<p>第一工作小組</p>","pre":"提升意識之事項：溝通、教育與大眾意識\n\n","en":[10]},{"md":"溝通、教育與大眾意識\n第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案","html":"<p>溝通、教育與大眾意識<br />\n第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案</p>","en":[11,12]},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"**回顧**其2024年11月1日的決議 16/10，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其2024年11月1日的決議 16/10，</p>","en":[14,15,16,17,18]},{"md":"1. **注意到**關於落實建議行動之進度報告，該行動旨在使生物多樣性公約之溝通、教育與大眾意識工作計畫¹與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要²相銜接，如文件 CBD/SBI/7/13 所載；","html":"<p>1. <strong>注意到</strong>關於落實建議行動之進度報告，該行動旨在使生物多樣性公約之溝通、教育與大眾意識工作計畫¹與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要²相銜接，如文件 CBD/SBI/7/13 所載；</p>","en":[19]},{"md":"2. **歡迎**南非於2026年以「在地行動，全球影響」為主題，成功舉辦國際生物多樣性日全球慶祝活動；","html":"<p>2. <strong>歡迎</strong>南非於2026年以「在地行動，全球影響」為主題，成功舉辦國際生物多樣性日全球慶祝活動；</p>","en":[20]},{"md":"3. **重申**其於決議 16/10 第6(c)小段對執行秘書之請求，即在第十八次及第十九次會議期間持續審查溝通、教育與大眾意識之議題；","html":"<p>3. <strong>重申</strong>其於決議 16/10 第6(c)小段對執行秘書之請求，即在第十八次及第十九次會議期間持續審查溝通、教育與大眾意識之議題；</p>","en":[21]},{"md":"4. **歡迎**本決議附件所含之生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案，並**建議**其使用，包括作為進一步投入之基礎，並**注意到**該文件為一份將會進一步發展的動態文件；","html":"<p>4. <strong>歡迎</strong>本決議附件所含之生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案，並<strong>建議</strong>其使用，包括作為進一步投入之基礎，並<strong>注意到</strong>該文件為一份將會進一步發展的動態文件；</p>","en":[22]},{"md":"[5. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府，[使用] [並落實] 生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案，以支持達成綱要目標與指標，以及實現與自然和諧共處之世界願景所需之轉型行動；]","html":"<p>[5. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府，[使用] [並落實] 生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案，以支持達成綱要目標與指標，以及實現與自然和諧共處之世界願景所需之轉型行動；]</p>","en":[23]},{"md":"6. **邀請**締約方、其他政府、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人，透過同儕審查程序提供投入，以進一步發展全球行動計畫；","html":"<p>6. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人，透過同儕審查程序提供投入，以進一步發展全球行動計畫；</p>","en":[24]},{"md":"---\n¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n² 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n² 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[25,26]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p002.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"7. Invites Parties, other Governments and [actors other than national Governments][other relevant stakeholders] to consider providing adequate, predictable and accessible technical and financial support for the development, uptake and implementation of the draft global plan of action, including in response to the needs of developing countries, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States among them, [by, inter alia, providing dedicated and easily accessible resources to indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth for such education activities as community-led education initiatives] [in accordance with national legislation and through appropriate national mechanisms];"},{"t":"8. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources and in consultation with the Informal Advisory Committee on Communication, Education and Public Awareness:"},{"t":"(a) action;"},{"t":"To conduct an inclusive and transparent peer review to further develop the plan of"},{"t":"(b) To submit, further to the peer review, an updated version of the draft global plan of action for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to its consideration at the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(c) To keep abreast of developments in other relevant international education initiatives and processes, [such as the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization Greening Education Partnership, the United Nations Decade on Ecosystem Restoration, the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change Action for Climate Empowerment and the Programme for International Student Assessment climate literacy assessment,] with a view to encouraging appropriate cooperation in the development, implementation and promotion of communication, education and public awareness plans at the national level and under relevant international processes;"},{"t":"(d) To facilitate the sharing of open-access digital biodiversity education resources, including learning materials, virtual learning platforms and digital knowledge products in the six official languages of the United Nations, through the clearing-house mechanism, while respecting the rights of indigenous peoples and local communities, as applicable;"},{"t":"9. Encourages Parties, taking into account national circumstances and legislation:"},{"t":"(a) To integrate education on biodiversity in national biodiversity strategies and action plans, where applicable [and in a manner consistent with][, and] national and subnational educational plans, as appropriate, taking into consideration the outcomes of the first global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Framework and building on existing education-related monitoring frameworks, including by considering formal, non-formal and informal education programmes and initiatives;"},{"t":"(b) To establish or strengthen, as appropriate, national mechanisms or platforms for coordinating biodiversity communication, education and public awareness across relevant ministries, educational institutions, scientific organizations and other stakeholders in order to promote a coherent implementation of the global plan of action;"},{"t":"(c) To establish or strengthen, as appropriate, mechanisms for translating scientific and technical biodiversity information into policy-relevant and practical communication products that can support decision-making, education and public engagement;"},{"t":"(d) To mainstream biodiversity across formal education curricula by integrating biodiversity and conservation concepts, ecosystem stewardship and care, and sustainable use considerations into relevant subjects and disciplines, taking into account national education systems and priorities."},{"t":"2/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"7.\n**邀請**締約方、其他政府及[國家政府以外之行為者][其他相關利害關係人]，考慮為全球行動計畫草案的制定、採用與執行提供充足、可預測且易於取得的技術與財務支持，包括回應開發中國家的需求，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，[除其他外，透過向原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年提供專屬且易於取得的資源，用於社群主導之教育倡議等教育活動] [並符合國家立法且透過適當之國家機制]；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及[國家政府以外之行為者][其他相關利害關係人]，考慮為全球行動計畫草案的制定、採用與執行提供充足、可預測且易於取得的技術與財務支持，包括回應開發中國家的需求，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，[除其他外，透過向原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年提供專屬且易於取得的資源，用於社群主導之教育倡議等教育活動] [並符合國家立法且透過適當之國家機制]；</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"8.\n**請求**執行秘書，在資源可用之情況下，並諮詢溝通、教育與大眾意識非正式諮詢委員會後：\n(a) 進行具包容性且透明的同儕審查，以進一步制定該行動計畫；\n(b) 在同儕審查後，提交全球行動計畫草案之更新版本，供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並以於第十八次締約方大會進行審議為目標；\n(c) 掌握其他相關國際教育倡議與進程之發展，[例如聯合國教科文組織綠色教育夥伴關係、聯合國生態系復育十年、聯合國氣候變遷綱要公約之氣候賦權行動，以及國際學生能力評量之氣候素養評量]，以期鼓勵在國家層級及相關國際進程下，針對溝通、教育與大眾意識計畫之制定、執行與推廣進行適當合作；\n(d) 透過資訊交換機制，促進以聯合國六種官方語言呈現之開放取得生物多樣性數位教育資源之分享，包括學習教材、虛擬學習平台與數位知識產品，同時在適用情況下尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>執行秘書，在資源可用之情況下，並諮詢溝通、教育與大眾意識非正式諮詢委員會後：<br />\n(a) 進行具包容性且透明的同儕審查，以進一步制定該行動計畫；<br />\n(b) 在同儕審查後，提交全球行動計畫草案之更新版本，供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議，並以於第十八次締約方大會進行審議為目標；<br />\n(c) 掌握其他相關國際教育倡議與進程之發展，[例如聯合國教科文組織綠色教育夥伴關係、聯合國生態系復育十年、聯合國氣候變遷綱要公約之氣候賦權行動，以及國際學生能力評量之氣候素養評量]，以期鼓勵在國家層級及相關國際進程下，針對溝通、教育與大眾意識計畫之制定、執行與推廣進行適當合作；<br />\n(d) 透過資訊交換機制，促進以聯合國六種官方語言呈現之開放取得生物多樣性數位教育資源之分享，包括學習教材、虛擬學習平台與數位知識產品，同時在適用情況下尊重原住民族與地方社區之權利；</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"9.\n**鼓勵**締約方在考慮國家情況與立法之情況下：\n(a) 在適用的情況下，將生物多樣性教育整合至國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫中，[且其方式應與][，以及]國家與次國家級教育計畫保持一致，並視適當情況，考慮綱要執行集體進展之第一次全球審查結果，並基於現有的教育相關監測架構，包括透過考慮正式、非正式與非正規教育計畫與倡議；\n(b) 視適當情況，建立或強化國家機制或平台，以協調相關部會、教育機構、科學組織及其他利害關係人之間之生物多樣性溝通、教育與大眾意識，以促進全球行動計畫之一致性執行；\n(c) 視適當情況，建立或強化機制，將科學與技術性的生物多樣性資訊轉化為具政策相關性且實用的溝通產品，以支持決策、教育與大眾參與；\n(d) 透過將生物多樣性與保育概念、生態系管理與照護，以及永續利用之考量納入相關科目與學科，並考慮國家教育體系與優先事項，將生物多樣性主流化於正式教育課程中。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方在考慮國家情況與立法之情況下：<br />\n(a) 在適用的情況下，將生物多樣性教育整合至國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫中，[且其方式應與][，以及]國家與次國家級教育計畫保持一致，並視適當情況，考慮綱要執行集體進展之第一次全球審查結果，並基於現有的教育相關監測架構，包括透過考慮正式、非正式與非正規教育計畫與倡議；<br />\n(b) 視適當情況，建立或強化國家機制或平台，以協調相關部會、教育機構、科學組織及其他利害關係人之間之生物多樣性溝通、教育與大眾意識，以促進全球行動計畫之一致性執行；<br />\n(c) 視適當情況，建立或強化機制，將科學與技術性的生物多樣性資訊轉化為具政策相關性且實用的溝通產品，以支持決策、教育與大眾參與；<br />\n(d) 透過將生物多樣性與保育概念、生態系管理與照護，以及永續利用之考量納入相關科目與學科，並考慮國家教育體系與優先事項，將生物多樣性主流化於正式教育課程中。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p003.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Annex"},{"t":"Draft global plan of action for education on biodiversity"},{"t":"I. Background and context"},{"t":"1. Pursuant to the request contained in decision 16/10 of 1 November 2024 of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity,3 and in line with the suggested actions to align the programme of work on communication, education and public awareness with the KunmingMontreal Global Biodiversity Framework 4 contained in the annex to the decision, the Executive Secretary prepared the global plan of action for education on biodiversity through a collaborative and participatory process involving consultations with Parties, observers, relevant organizations, indigenous peoples and local communities, and women and youth representatives, including the Global Youth Biodiversity Network. The United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization played a leading role in facilitating consultations and technical inputs, consistent with its mandate on education."},{"t":"2. The global plan is intended to strengthen knowledge, values, competences and skills in support of behavioural change, and individual and collective action by fostering agency, stewardship and transformative leadership consistent with the 2030 targets of the Framework, in accordance with national priorities and circumstances."},{"t":"3. Inputs provided through consultations, including through the Informal Advisory Committee on Communication, Education and Public Awareness, have informed the structure, expected outcomes, priority areas and indicative actions of the global plan."},{"t":"II."},{"t":"Purpose"},{"t":"4. The purpose of the global plan is to support the effective implementation of the Framework and to contribute measurably to the achievement of its goals and targets, including the actions related to communication, education, awareness and uptake contained in section K of the Framework, by strengthening education on biodiversity as a strategic enabling condition for transformative change5 and fostering long-term societal engagement and action. Education on biodiversity is to be understood as education that fosters views, structures and practices that are consistent with living in harmony with nature and that addresses the direct, underlying and structural causes of biodiversity loss, going beyond the transmission of knowledge and awareness alone."},{"t":"5. The global plan provides a flexible framework with interconnected outcomes to advance education on biodiversity through formal, non-formal and informal learning, in support of the 2030 targets and the Framework. It is aimed at enabling informed decision-making and individual and collective action by strengthening knowledge, values and skills and by helping people to understand the relevance of biodiversity to their daily life, while supporting action competence, systems thinking and active participation in biodiversity conservation."},{"t":"6. The global plan covers the period up to 2030, coinciding with the time frame of the targets of the Framework. Its implementation is to be reviewed at the eighteenth and nineteenth meetings of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"7. The global plan is intended to support Parties, subnational governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and other relevant stakeholders and actors, in accordance with national legislation and priorities, in advancing education on biodiversity and actions to conserve and restore biodiversity sustainably, through voluntary, nationally driven implementation supported by partnerships and the meaningful participation of indigenous people and local communities, women,"},{"t":"3 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"4 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"5 See Karen O’Brien, Lucas Garibaldi and Arun Agrawal, eds., The Thematic Assessment Report on the Underlying Causes of"},{"t":"Biodiversity Loss and the Determinants of Transformative Change and Options for Achieving the 2050 Vision for Biodiversity (Bonn, Secretariat of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services, 2024)."},{"t":"3/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"附件\n生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案","html":"<p>附件<br />\n生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"I.","html":"<p>I.</p>","pre":"附件\n生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫草案\n\n","en":[3]},{"md":"背景與脈絡","html":"<p>背景與脈絡</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"1.\n根據生物多樣性公約締約方大會 2024 年 11 月 1 日決議 16/10 所提出的請求，³ 並配合該決議附件中所建議之旨在使溝通、教育與大眾意識工作計畫與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》⁴ 保持一致的行動，執行秘書透過一個協作且參與式的程序，編製了生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫；該程序包括與締約方、觀察員、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區，以及包括全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）在內的女性與青年代表進行諮商。聯合國教育、科學及文化組織在其教育職能範圍內，在促進諮商與技術投入方面發揮了領導作用。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據生物多樣性公約締約方大會 2024 年 11 月 1 日決議 16/10 所提出的請求，³ 並配合該決議附件中所建議之旨在使溝通、教育與大眾意識工作計畫與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》⁴ 保持一致的行動，執行秘書透過一個協作且參與式的程序，編製了生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫；該程序包括與締約方、觀察員、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區，以及包括全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）在內的女性與青年代表進行諮商。聯合國教育、科學及文化組織在其教育職能範圍內，在促進諮商與技術投入方面發揮了領導作用。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"2.\n該全球計畫旨在強化知識、價值觀、能力與技能，以支持行為改變，並透過促進自主性、管理責任與轉型領導力，配合《綱要》2030 年標的，並根據國家優先事項與情況，支持個人與集體行動。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n該全球計畫旨在強化知識、價值觀、能力與技能，以支持行為改變，並透過促進自主性、管理責任與轉型領導力，配合《綱要》2030 年標的，並根據國家優先事項與情況，支持個人與集體行動。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"3.\n透過諮商（包括透過溝通、教育與大眾意識非正式諮詢委員會）所提供的投入，已為全球計畫的結構、預期成果、優先領域及指標性行動提供了資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n透過諮商（包括透過溝通、教育與大眾意識非正式諮詢委員會）所提供的投入，已為全球計畫的結構、預期成果、優先領域及指標性行動提供了資訊。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"II.","html":"<p>II.</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"目的","html":"<p>目的</p>","pre":"域及指標性行動提供了資訊。\n\nII.\n\n","en":[8]},{"md":"4.\n全球計畫之目的，在於透過強化生物多樣性教育，將其作為轉型變革的策略性促成條件，⁵ 並促進長期的社會參與及行動，藉此支持《綱要》的有效實施，並為達成其目標與標的做出可衡量的貢獻，包括《綱要》K 節中所包含的與溝通、教育、意識及採納相關的行動。生物多樣性教育應被理解為一種能促進與自然和諧共處之觀點、結構與實踐的教育，且其範疇應超越單純的知識傳遞與意識提升，進而應對生物多樣性流失的直接、潛在及結構性原因。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n全球計畫之目的，在於透過強化生物多樣性教育，將其作為轉型變革的策略性促成條件，⁵ 並促進長期的社會參與及行動，藉此支持《綱要》的有效實施，並為達成其目標與標的做出可衡量的貢獻，包括《綱要》K 節中所包含的與溝通、教育、意識及採納相關的行動。生物多樣性教育應被理解為一種能促進與自然和諧共處之觀點、結構與實踐的教育，且其範疇應超越單純的知識傳遞與意識提升，進而應對生物多樣性流失的直接、潛在及結構性原因。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"5.\n全球計畫提供了一個具有相互關聯成果的彈性框架，透過正式、非正式及非正規學習來推進生物多樣性教育，以支持 2030 年標的與《綱要》。其目標是透過強化知識、價值觀與技能，並幫助人們理解生物多樣性與其日常生活的相關性，來實現知情決策與個人及集體行動，同時支持行動能力、系統性思考以及對生物多樣性保育的積極參與。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n全球計畫提供了一個具有相互關聯成果的彈性框架，透過正式、非正式及非正規學習來推進生物多樣性教育，以支持 2030 年標的與《綱要》。其目標是透過強化知識、價值觀與技能，並幫助人們理解生物多樣性與其日常生活的相關性，來實現知情決策與個人及集體行動，同時支持行動能力、系統性思考以及對生物多樣性保育的積極參與。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"6.\n全球計畫涵蓋至 2030 年，與《綱要》標的的時間範圍一致。其執行情況應在第十八與第十九屆締約方大會期間進行審查。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n全球計畫涵蓋至 2030 年，與《綱要》標的的時間範圍一致。其執行情況應在第十八與第十九屆締約方大會期間進行審查。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"7.\n全球計畫旨在根據國家立法與優先事項，透過由夥伴關係以及原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之實質參與所支持的、自願且由國家驅動的實施，支持締約方、次國家級政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他相關利害關係人與行為者，推進生物多樣性教育，以及永續保育與復育生物多樣性的行動。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n全球計畫旨在根據國家立法與優先事項，透過由夥伴關係以及原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之實質參與所支持的、自願且由國家驅動的實施，支持締約方、次國家級政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他相關利害關係人與行為者，推進生物多樣性教育，以及永續保育與復育生物多樣性的行動。</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[12]},{"md":"³ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n⁴ 決議 15/4，附件。\n⁵ 參見 Karen O’Brien, Lucas Garibaldi and Arun Agrawal, eds., *The Thematic Assessment Report on the Underlying Causes of Biodiversity Loss and the Determinants of Transformative Change and Options for Achieving the 2050 Vision for Biodiversity* (Bonn, Secretariat of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services, 2024)。","html":"<p>³ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n⁴ 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n⁵ 參見 Karen O’Brien, Lucas Garibaldi and Arun Agrawal, eds., <em>The Thematic Assessment Report on the Underlying Causes of Biodiversity Loss and the Determinants of Transformative Change and Options for Achieving the 2050 Vision for Biodiversity</em> (Bonn, Secretariat of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services, 2024)。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p004.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"youth and civil society. It should also inform related educational efforts, including those addressing the links among biodiversity, climate change, ecosystem restoration and sustainable development, while maintaining its primary focus under the Convention."},{"t":"8. The implementation of the global plan should be adapted to diverse national contexts, circumstances and priorities and carried out through approaches that are specific to national formal and non-formal educational systems, capacities and implementation pathways."},{"t":"III. Guiding principles for implementation"},{"t":"9. The implementation of the global plan is to be guided by the following principles, which are aligned with the Convention and the Framework and support coherent, voluntary and nationally driven implementation across diverse contexts:"},{"t":"(a) Education on biodiversity, including strengthening biodiversity literacy, values, competences and skills, as well as decision-making capacity and leadership in government, business, finance and society, underpins the achievement of the goals and targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"(b) Education on biodiversity is lifelong, takes place in formal, non-formal and informal contexts and involves a wide range of actors, including indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, and locations, including institutions, sectors, communities and social spaces, in line with a whole-of-society approach;"},{"t":"(c) Approaches to education on biodiversity should be pluralistic, holistic, genderresponsive and equitable, recognize and integrate diverse knowledge systems and world views, including those of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, and promote cocreation, intercultural learning and intergenerational knowledge exchange;"},{"t":"(d) Actions to advance education on biodiversity should be context-specific, inclusive and adaptive and reflect national priorities, educational systems, institutional arrangements and diverse cultural, social, economic and ecological settings, including at the local, subnational, national and regional levels;"},{"t":"(e) Education on biodiversity should be grounded in empirical place- and project-based learning in order to foster direct engagement with natural, cultural and living environments, and engage learners in specific, locally relevant, problem-solving activities, which could be complemented by online education;"},{"t":"(f) Actions to advance education on biodiversity should foster partnerships and collaboration among Parties, subnational governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth, the private sector and other relevant stakeholders and actors, in support of collective action;"},{"t":"(g) Implementation of the global plan should be gender-responsive, consistent with decision 15/11 of 19 December 2022 and Target 23 of the Framework."},{"t":"IV. Results framework"},{"t":"10. The results framework for the global plan comprises three interrelated expected outcomes that are supported by five priority areas for action and three cross-cutting enabling conditions for implementation, as shown in the figure below. Together, those elements form an integrated framework in which individual learning, educator and system capacity, and the broader enabling conditions required for sustained implementation are connected."},{"t":"Results framework for the global plan of action for education on biodiversity Expected outcomes"},{"t":"1. Strengthened understanding"},{"t":"of the connection with and"},{"t":"stewardship of biodiversity"},{"t":"4/12"},{"t":"2. Strengthened educator and"},{"t":"system capacity to foster"},{"t":"understanding of biodiversity"},{"t":"3. Strengthened enabling"},{"t":"conditions for the"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"青年與公民社會。其亦應為相關教育工作提供資訊，包括處理生物多樣性、氣候變遷、生態系復育與永續發展之間聯繫的工作，同時維持其在《公約》下的主要焦點。","html":"<p>青年與公民社會。其亦應為相關教育工作提供資訊，包括處理生物多樣性、氣候變遷、生態系復育與永續發展之間聯繫的工作，同時維持其在《公約》下的主要焦點。</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"8.\n全球計畫的實施應適應不同的國家情境、情況與優先事項，並透過特定於國家正式與非正式教育系統、能力及實施路徑的方法來進行。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n全球計畫的實施應適應不同的國家情境、情況與優先事項，並透過特定於國家正式與非正式教育系統、能力及實施路徑的方法來進行。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"III. 實施指導原則","html":"<p>III. 實施指導原則</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"9.\n全球計畫的實施應受以下原則指導，這些原則與《公約》及《綱要》保持一致，並支持在不同情境下進行一致、自願且由國家驅動的實施：\n(a) 生物多樣性教育，包括強化生物多樣性素養、價值觀、能力與技能，以及政府、企業、金融與社會的決策能力與領導力，是達成《綱要》目標與指標的基礎；\n(b) 生物多樣性教育是終身的，發生於正式、非正式與非正規情境中，並涉及廣泛的行為者，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，以及包括機構、部門、社區與社會空間在內的場域，並符合全社會參與的方法；\n(c) 生物多樣性教育的方法應具多元性、整體性、性別回應性與公平性，認可並整合多元的知識體系與世界觀，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的知識體系，並促進共同創造、跨文化學習與跨世代知識交流；\n(d) 推動生物多樣性教育的行動應具特定情境性、包容性與適應性，並反映國家優先事項、教育系統、制度安排以及多樣的文化、社會、經濟與生態背景，包括地方、次國家級、國家與區域層級；\n(e) 生物多樣性教育應以基於地點與專案的實證學習為基礎，以促進與自然、文化及生命環境的直接參與，並讓學習者參與特定且具地方相關性的問題解決活動，且此類學習可由線上教育作為補充；\n(f) 推動生物多樣性教育的行動應促進締約方、次國家級政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、私營部門及其他相關利害關係人與行為者之間的夥伴關係與合作，以支持集體行動；\n(g) 全球計畫的實施應具性別回應性，並與 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/11 及《綱要》目標 23 保持一致。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n全球計畫的實施應受以下原則指導，這些原則與《公約》及《綱要》保持一致，並支持在不同情境下進行一致、自願且由國家驅動的實施：<br />\n(a) 生物多樣性教育，包括強化生物多樣性素養、價值觀、能力與技能，以及政府、企業、金融與社會的決策能力與領導力，是達成《綱要》目標與指標的基礎；<br />\n(b) 生物多樣性教育是終身的，發生於正式、非正式與非正規情境中，並涉及廣泛的行為者，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，以及包括機構、部門、社區與社會空間在內的場域，並符合全社會參與的方法；<br />\n(c) 生物多樣性教育的方法應具多元性、整體性、性別回應性與公平性，認可並整合多元的知識體系與世界觀，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年的知識體系，並促進共同創造、跨文化學習與跨世代知識交流；<br />\n(d) 推動生物多樣性教育的行動應具特定情境性、包容性與適應性，並反映國家優先事項、教育系統、制度安排以及多樣的文化、社會、經濟與生態背景，包括地方、次國家級、國家與區域層級；<br />\n(e) 生物多樣性教育應以基於地點與專案的實證學習為基礎，以促進與自然、文化及生命環境的直接參與，並讓學習者參與特定且具地方相關性的問題解決活動，且此類學習可由線上教育作為補充；<br />\n(f) 推動生物多樣性教育的行動應促進締約方、次國家級政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、私營部門及其他相關利害關係人與行為者之間的夥伴關係與合作，以支持集體行動；<br />\n(g) 全球計畫的實施應具性別回應性，並與 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/11 及《綱要》目標 23 保持一致。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"IV. 結果架構","html":"<p>IV. 結果架構</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"10. 全球計畫的結果架構包含三個相互關聯的預期成果，並由五個優先行動領域與三個跨領域的實施賦能條件所支持，如下圖所示。這些要素共同構成了一個整合架構，其中個人學習、教育者與系統能力，以及持續實施所需的更廣泛賦能條件皆相互連結。","html":"<p>10. 全球計畫的結果架構包含三個相互關聯的預期成果，並由五個優先行動領域與三個跨領域的實施賦能條件所支持，如下圖所示。這些要素共同構成了一個整合架構，其中個人學習、教育者與系統能力，以及持續實施所需的更廣泛賦能條件皆相互連結。</p>","en":[13,14]},{"md":"生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫結果架構","html":"<p>生物多樣性教育全球行動計畫結果架構</p>","en":[15,16,17,18]},{"md":"| 預期成果 | 　 | 　 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1. 強化對生物多樣性之連結與守護的理解 | 2. 強化教育者與系統促進對生物多樣性理解的能力 | 3. 強化有利於該 |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">預期成果</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">1. 強化對生物多樣性之連結與守護的理解</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">2. 強化教育者與系統促進對生物多樣性理解的能力</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">3. 強化有利於該</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[19,20,21,22]},{"md":"4/12","html":"<p>4/12</p>","en":[23]}],"csv":[{"f":"CBD-COP-17-WGI-CRP6/p004-t1.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p005.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"implementation of policies"},{"t":"supporting the plan of action"},{"t":"Priority areas for action"},{"t":"Fostering humannature"},{"t":"connectedness"},{"t":"and stewardship"},{"t":"actions"},{"t":"Pluralistic,"},{"t":"holistic and"},{"t":"equitable"},{"t":"education"},{"t":"Enhancing and"},{"t":"stewardship of"},{"t":"Capacity-building"},{"t":"coordination,"},{"t":"for educators and"},{"t":"platforms and"},{"t":"learning systems"},{"t":"knowledge"},{"t":"exchange"},{"t":"Embedding"},{"t":"education on"},{"t":"biodiversity in"},{"t":"policy and"},{"t":"curriculum"},{"t":"frameworks and"},{"t":"infrastructure"},{"t":"Cross-cutting enabling conditions for implementation"},{"t":"Lifelong, life-wide and lifedeep learning"},{"t":"Whole-of-society engagement"},{"t":"Sustainable financing and"},{"t":"incentives"},{"t":"11. The three cross-cutting enabling conditions support the implementation of actions under the priority areas and the achievement of the expected outcomes by strengthening the institutional, social and learning environments necessary for sustained progress. The enabling conditions relate to the broader systemic and societal foundations required to support implementation at scale and over time. They address lifelong, life-wide and life-deep learning; whole-of-society engagement, ensuring the meaningful participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, and sustainable financing and incentives."},{"t":"12. The expected outcomes reflect the understanding that transformative change requires action across multiple dimensions, including relationships between people and biodiversity, the development of active global citizenship competences, the capacity of educators and learning systems to support learners across diverse contexts and the broader institutional, policy and financing conditions necessary to ensuring coherence, scale and long-term impact. The outcomes are mutually reinforcing and are not intended to be pursued in isolation."},{"t":"13. Expected outcome 1, on strengthened understanding of the connection with and stewardship of biodiversity, follows from the recognition of the ability of education on biodiversity to strengthen knowledge, values and skills. The aim is to enable learners and communities to understand the relevance of biodiversity to their lives, adopt supporting behaviours, become active global citizens and act in ways that contribute to sustaining biodiversity."},{"t":"14. Expected outcome 2, on strengthened educator and system capacity, follows from the recognition that education on biodiversity requires both strengthened educator capacity and more coherent system-wide approaches. The aim is to support the development of professional educators, including teachers, trainers, civil society educators, community knowledge holders and other learning facilitators, while strengthening the institutions, platforms and learning systems for biodiversity education in order to reach learners in diverse settings."},{"t":"15. Expected outcome 3, on strengthened enabling conditions for implementation, follows from the recognition that lasting impact depends on institutional arrangements, policy coherence and sustained resourcing that extend beyond individual programmes and political cycles. Achieving the outcome and the consistent and effective contribution of biodiversity education to biodiversityrelated goals will require the enabling conditions to be strengthened across national contexts."},{"t":"16. The results framework is accompanied by indicators and monitoring mechanisms that enable the assessment of progress, outcomes and contributions to the goals and targets of the Framework."},{"t":"V. Priority areas for action: objectives and indicative actions"},{"t":"17. Objectives and indicative actions for each of the priority areas and cross-cutting enabling conditions provide pathways for implementing the global plan in support of the Framework. 5/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 　 | 　 | 　 | 支持行動計畫之政策執行 | 　 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 行動優先領域 |  |  |  |  |\n| 促進人與自然的連結與管理行動 | 多元、整體且公平的教育 | 教育者與學習系統之能力建構 | 強化協調、平台與知識交流及其管理 | 將生物多樣性教育嵌入政策與課程架構及基礎設施 |\n| 執行之跨領域使能條件 |  |  |  |  |\n| 終身、全方位且深層的學習 | 全社會參與 |  | 永續財務與誘因 |  |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">支持行動計畫之政策執行</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">　</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">行動優先領域</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">促進人與自然的連結與管理行動</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">多元、整體且公平的教育</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">教育者與學習系統之能力建構</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">強化協調、平台與知識交流及其管理</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">將生物多樣性教育嵌入政策與課程架構及基礎設施</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">執行之跨領域使能條件</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">終身、全方位且深層的學習</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">全社會參與</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">永續財務與誘因</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"11. 三項跨領域使能條件透過強化持續進展所需之制度、社會與學習環境，以支持優先領域下行動之執行及預期成果之達成。此等使能條件涉及支持大規模且長期執行所需之更廣泛系統性與社會性基礎。其涵蓋終身、全方位且深層的學習；全社會參與，確保原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之實質參與；以及永續財務與誘因機制。","html":"<p>11. 三項跨領域使能條件透過強化持續進展所需之制度、社會與學習環境，以支持優先領域下行動之執行及預期成果之達成。此等使能條件涉及支持大規模且長期執行所需之更廣泛系統性與社會性基礎。其涵蓋終身、全方位且深層的學習；全社會參與，確保原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之實質參與；以及永續財務與誘因機制。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"12. 預期成果反映了以下理解：轉型變革需要跨維度的行動，包括人與生物多樣性之間的關係、主動全球公民素養之發展、教育者與學習系統在多元情境下支持學習者之能力，以及確保一致性、規模化與長期影響所需之更廣泛制度、政策與財務條件。各項成果相互強化，且並非旨在孤立地追求。","html":"<p>12. 預期成果反映了以下理解：轉型變革需要跨維度的行動，包括人與生物多樣性之間的關係、主動全球公民素養之發展、教育者與學習系統在多元情境下支持學習者之能力，以及確保一致性、規模化與長期影響所需之更廣泛制度、政策與財務條件。各項成果相互強化，且並非旨在孤立地追求。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]},{"md":"13. 關於強化對生物多樣性連結與管理之理解之預期成果 1，源於認可生物多樣性教育具有強化知識、價值觀與技能之能力。其目標在於使學習者與社區能夠理解生物多樣性與其生活之關聯性、採取支持性行為、成為積極的全球公民，並以有助於維護生物多樣性之方式行動。","html":"<p>13. 關於強化對生物多樣性連結與管理之理解之預期成果 1，源於認可生物多樣性教育具有強化知識、價值觀與技能之能力。其目標在於使學習者與社區能夠理解生物多樣性與其生活之關聯性、採取支持性行為、成為積極的全球公民，並以有助於維護生物多樣性之方式行動。</p>","en":[24,25,26,27,28]},{"md":"14. 關於強化教育者與系統能力之預期成果 2，源於認可生物多樣性教育需要強化教育者能力以及更具一致性的系統性方法。其目標在於支持專業教育者之發展，包括教師、培訓師、公民社會教育者、社區知識持有者及其他學習促進者，同時強化生物多樣性教育之制度、平台與學習系統，以便觸及不同情境下的學習者。","html":"<p>14. 關於強化教育者與系統能力之預期成果 2，源於認可生物多樣性教育需要強化教育者能力以及更具一致性的系統性方法。其目標在於支持專業教育者之發展，包括教師、培訓師、公民社會教育者、社區知識持有者及其他學習促進者，同時強化生物多樣性教育之制度、平台與學習系統，以便觸及不同情境下的學習者。</p>","en":[29,30,31,32,33]},{"md":"15. 關於強化執行之使能條件之預期成果 3，源於認可持久的影響取決於超越個別計畫與政治週期的制度安排、政策一致性及持續性的資源投入。達成此成果，以及使生物多樣性教育對生物多樣性相關目標做出一致且有效的貢獻，將需要於國家情境下強化使能條件。","html":"<p>15. 關於強化執行之使能條件之預期成果 3，源於認可持久的影響取決於超越個別計畫與政治週期的制度安排、政策一致性及持續性的資源投入。達成此成果，以及使生物多樣性教育對生物多樣性相關目標做出一致且有效的貢獻，將需要於國家情境下強化使能條件。</p>","en":[34,35,36,37]},{"md":"16. 結果架構附有指標與監測機制，用以評估進展、成果以及對《綱要》目標與指標之貢獻。","html":"<p>16. 結果架構附有指標與監測機制，用以評估進展、成果以及對《綱要》目標與指標之貢獻。</p>","en":[38]},{"md":"V.","html":"<p>V.</p>","en":[38]},{"md":"行動優先領域：目標與指示性行動","html":"<p>行動優先領域：目標與指示性行動</p>","en":[39]},{"md":"17. 各項優先領域與跨領域使能條件之目標與指示性行動，為執行支持《綱要》之全球計畫提供了路徑。","html":"<p>17. 各項優先領域與跨領域使能條件之目標與指示性行動，為執行支持《綱要》之全球計畫提供了路徑。</p>","en":[40]}],"csv":[{"f":"CBD-COP-17-WGI-CRP6/p005-t2.csv","t":""}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p006.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"18. Tables 1 to 4 below contain the objectives, indicative actions, possible deliverables and indicative actors associated with each priority area and cross-cutting enabling condition. The priority areas are organized under the three expected outcomes described above. The indicative actions are intended to support voluntary and nationally driven implementation consistent with national priorities and capacities. Their implementation may also contribute to adaptive learning, monitoring and knowledge exchange over time."},{"t":"19. The Secretariat of the Convention is requested to work with Parties and relevant partners to develop voluntary, non-prescriptive guidance and indicators to help Parties to monitor and report on public access to, and use of, biodiversity education and information, building on national experience, including under Target 21 of the Framework."},{"t":"6/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"18. 下列表 1 至表 4 包含與各優先領域及跨領域使能條件相關的目標、指標性行動、可能的成果以及指標性行為者。優先領域依據上述所述之三個預期成果進行編排。指標性行動旨在支持符合國家優先事項與能力的自願性且由國家驅動之執行。其執行亦可能有助於隨著時間推移進行調適性學習、監測與知識交流。","html":"<p>18. 下列表 1 至表 4 包含與各優先領域及跨領域使能條件相關的目標、指標性行動、可能的成果以及指標性行為者。優先領域依據上述所述之三個預期成果進行編排。指標性行動旨在支持符合國家優先事項與能力的自願性且由國家驅動之執行。其執行亦可能有助於隨著時間推移進行調適性學習、監測與知識交流。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"19. **請求**公約秘書處與締約方及相關夥伴合作，制定自願性、非指令性的指引與指標，以協助締約方針對生物多樣性教育與資訊的公開取得與使用進行監測與報告，並以國家經驗為基礎，包括在綱要目標 21 之下。","html":"<p>19. <strong>請求</strong>公約秘書處與締約方及相關夥伴合作，制定自願性、非指令性的指引與指標，以協助締約方針對生物多樣性教育與資訊的公開取得與使用進行監測與報告，並以國家經驗為基礎，包括在綱要目標 21 之下。</p>","en":[2,3]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p007.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Table 1"},{"t":"Expected outcome 1: priority areas, objectives, indicative actions, possible deliverables and indicative actors Priority area"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"Fostering humannature connectedness and stewardship"},{"t":"actions"},{"t":"To strengthen lifelong"},{"t":"human-nature"},{"t":"connectedness and"},{"t":"active global"},{"t":"citizenship"},{"t":"competences"},{"t":"• Expand experiential, outdoor and place- and project-based learning across formal, non-formal and informal contexts, enhancing access to and sustainable interaction with nature"},{"t":"Non-prescriptive guidance, illustrative case studies, communitybased initiatives and learning resources, and examples of approaches that support behavioural change, including access to and sustainable interaction with nature"},{"t":"Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities,"},{"t":"women’s and youth"},{"t":"organizations, education"},{"t":"authorities and institutions, civil society, the private sector, scientists and relevant organizations"},{"t":"Co-created learning resources, interdisciplinary and cross-sectoral learning modules, learning materials in languages of indigenous peoples and local communities, localized learning materials and examples of good practice"},{"t":"Parties, educational authorities and institutions, indigenous peoples and local"},{"t":"communities, and women’s"},{"t":"and youth organizations"},{"t":"• Support early childhood, familybased and intergenerational learning • Promote cultural, artistic and storytelling approaches that foster emotional connections with biodiversity and nature"},{"t":"• Promote sustainable consumption, production and lifestyle"},{"t":"competencies that reduce pressures on biodiversity"},{"t":"• Promote the use of languages of indigenous peoples and local communities and rural and"},{"t":"community media, including community radio, in the design and delivery of biodiversity education materials, to reach underserved and remote populations"},{"t":"Pluralistic, holistic"},{"t":"and equitable"},{"t":"education"},{"t":"To promote pluralistic,"},{"t":"holistic and equitable"},{"t":"approaches to"},{"t":"education on"},{"t":"biodiversity, including"},{"t":"through genderresponsive"},{"t":"implementation"},{"t":"• Draw from scientific knowledge alongside diverse knowledge systems, including those of indigenous peoples and local communities"},{"t":"• Promote critical and systems thinking that addresses links among biodiversity, climate, health, human rights and sustainable development"},{"t":"7/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"表 1\n預期成果 1：優先領域、目標、指標性行動、可能之成果產出與指標性行為者\n優先領域","html":"<p>表 1<br />\n預期成果 1：優先領域、目標、指標性行動、可能之成果產出與指標性行為者<br />\n優先領域</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"目標","html":"<p>目標</p>","pre":"能之成果產出與指標性行為者\n優先領域\n\n","en":[3]},{"md":"指標性行動","html":"<p>指標性行動</p>","pre":"產出與指標性行為者\n優先領域\n\n目標\n\n","en":[4]},{"md":"可能之成果產出","html":"<p>可能之成果產出</p>","pre":"為者\n優先領域\n\n目標\n\n指標性行動\n\n","en":[5]},{"md":"指標性行為者","html":"<p>指標性行為者</p>","pre":"目標\n\n指標性行動\n\n可能之成果產出\n\n","en":[6]},{"md":"促進人與自然之連結與管理行動","html":"<p>促進人與自然之連結與管理行動</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"強化終身人與自然連結及積極全球公民素養之能力","html":"<p>強化終身人與自然連結及積極全球公民素養之能力</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"• 在正式、非正式及非正規情境下，擴大體驗式、戶外、以地點及專案為基礎之學習，以增進與自然之接觸及永續互動","html":"<p>• 在正式、非正式及非正規情境下，擴大體驗式、戶外、以地點及專案為基礎之學習，以增進與自然之接觸及永續互動</p>","en":[13,14,15]},{"md":"非規範性指引、說明性案例研究、以社區為基礎之倡議與學習資源，以及支持行為改變之方法範例，包括與自然之接觸及永續互動","html":"<p>非規範性指引、說明性案例研究、以社區為基礎之倡議與學習資源，以及支持行為改變之方法範例，包括與自然之接觸及永續互動</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、教育主管機關與機構、公民社會、私營部門、科學家及相關組織","html":"<p>締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、教育主管機關與機構、公民社會、私營部門、科學家及相關組織</p>","en":[17,18,19,20]},{"md":"共同開發之學習資源、跨學科與跨部門之學習模組、以原住民族與地方社區語言編製之學習教材、在地化學習教材及優良實務範例","html":"<p>共同開發之學習資源、跨學科與跨部門之學習模組、以原住民族與地方社區語言編製之學習教材、在地化學習教材及優良實務範例</p>","en":[21]},{"md":"締約方、教育主管機關與機構、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織","html":"<p>締約方、教育主管機關與機構、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織</p>","en":[22,23,24]},{"md":"• 支持幼兒、以家庭為基礎及跨世代之學習\n• 推廣文化、藝術與說故事之方法，以促進與生物多樣性及自然之情感連結\n• 推廣能減輕生物多樣性壓力之永續消費、生產與生活方式素養\n• 在生物多樣性教育教材之設計與傳遞中，推廣使用原住民族與地方社區之語言以及農村與社區媒體（包括社區電台），以觸及服務不足及偏遠之族群","html":"<p>• 支持幼兒、以家庭為基礎及跨世代之學習<br />\n• 推廣文化、藝術與說故事之方法，以促進與生物多樣性及自然之情感連結<br />\n• 推廣能減輕生物多樣性壓力之永續消費、生產與生活方式素養<br />\n• 在生物多樣性教育教材之設計與傳遞中，推廣使用原住民族與地方社區之語言以及農村與社區媒體（包括社區電台），以觸及服務不足及偏遠之族群</p>","en":[25,26,27,28,29]},{"md":"多元、整體且公平之教育","html":"<p>多元、整體且公平之教育</p>","en":[30,31,32]},{"md":"透過包含性別回應之執行，推廣生物多樣性教育之多元、整體且公平方法","html":"<p>透過包含性別回應之執行，推廣生物多樣性教育之多元、整體且公平方法</p>","en":[33,34,35,36,37]},{"md":"• 結合科學知識與多元知識體系，包括原住民族與地方社區之知識體系\n• 推廣探討生物多樣性、氣候、健康、人權與永續發展之間關聯之批判性與系統性思考\n• 支援發展能強化能動性與負責任行動之能力\n• 支援具文化相關性且符合特定情境之學習方法，並將文化多樣性整合至教育中，包括傳統與地方管理實務\n• 除了知識傳遞方法外，亦支援能使學習者識別並針對生物多樣性流失之結構性與潛在原因採取行動的批判性與轉型式教學法","html":"<p>• 結合科學知識與多元知識體系，包括原住民族與地方社區之知識體系<br />\n• 推廣探討生物多樣性、氣候、健康、人權與永續發展之間關聯之批判性與系統性思考<br />\n• 支援發展能強化能動性與負責任行動之能力<br />\n• 支援具文化相關性且符合特定情境之學習方法，並將文化多樣性整合至教育中，包括傳統與地方管理實務<br />\n• 除了知識傳遞方法外，亦支援能使學習者識別並針對生物多樣性流失之結構性與潛在原因採取行動的批判性與轉型式教學法</p>","en":[38,39,40,41,42]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p008.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Priority area"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"• Support the development of competences that strengthen agency and responsible action"},{"t":"• Support culturally relevant and context-specific learning approaches and integrate cultural diversity in education, including in traditional and local management practices • Support critical and transformative pedagogy that enables learners to identify and act on the structural and underlying causes of biodiversity loss, in addition to knowledgetransfer approaches"},{"t":"Table 2"},{"t":"Expected outcome 2: priority areas, objectives, indicative actions, possible deliverables and indicative actors Priority area"},{"t":"Objectives"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"Capacity-building for"},{"t":"educators and"},{"t":"learning systems"},{"t":"To strengthen the capacity of educators and learning systems to support education on"},{"t":"biodiversity"},{"t":"• Support pre-service and in-service professional development"},{"t":"Voluntary training"},{"t":"opportunities, educator"},{"t":"toolkits, and peer-learning networks and exchanges"},{"t":"Parties, teacher education institutions, civil society, including indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth organizations and other relevant organizations"},{"t":"• Support the integration of biodiversity competencies into national teacher qualification standards and teacher licensing systems"},{"t":"• Facilitate the creation and strengthening of communities of practice and peer-learning networks • Improve access to tools and resources for educators across learning contexts"},{"t":"8/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 優先領域 | 目標 | 指示性行動 | 可能的成果物 | 指示性行為者 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 教育者與學習系統之能力建構 | 強化教育者與學習系統支援生物多樣性教育之能力 | • 支援職前與在職專業發展<br>• 支援將生物多樣性素養整合至國家教師資格標準與教師執照制度中<br>• 促進實務社群與同儕學習網絡之建立與強化<br>• 改善各學習情境下教育者取得工具與資源之管道 | 自願性培訓機會、教育者工具包，以及同儕學習網絡與交流 | 締約方、師資培育機構、包含原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關組織之公民社會 |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">優先領域</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">可能的成果物</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行為者</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">教育者與學習系統之能力建構</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">強化教育者與學習系統支援生物多樣性教育之能力</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 支援職前與在職專業發展<br>• 支援將生物多樣性素養整合至國家教師資格標準與教師執照制度中<br>• 促進實務社群與同儕學習網絡之建立與強化<br>• 改善各學習情境下教育者取得工具與資源之管道</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">自願性培訓機會、教育者工具包，以及同儕學習網絡與交流</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、師資培育機構、包含原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關組織之公民社會</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"表 2\n預期成果 2：優先領域、目標、指示性行動、可能的成果物與指示性行為者","html":"<p>表 2<br />\n預期成果 2：優先領域、目標、指示性行動、可能的成果物與指示性行為者</p>","en":[21,22,23,24,25]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p009.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Priority area"},{"t":"Objectives"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"To strengthen the institutional integration of education on biodiversity within"},{"t":"governance, standards and"},{"t":"quality assurance frameworks"},{"t":"• Integrate biodiversity into teacher competency standards and"},{"t":"accreditation processes"},{"t":"Illustrative competency"},{"t":"frameworks, curriculum"},{"t":"review references, and"},{"t":"institutional selfassessment tools and guidance"},{"t":"Parties, educational authorities, accreditation bodies, indigenous peoples and local communities, and women’s and youth organizations"},{"t":"• Align the objectives of education on biodiversity with curriculum review cycles and assessment frameworks, including the Programme for International Student Assessment climate literacy assessment • Incorporate education on biodiversity into institutional development plans • Strengthen professional training on the conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity"},{"t":"Table 3"},{"t":"Expected outcome 3: priority areas, objectives, indicative actions, possible deliverables and indicative actors Priority area"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"Enhancing"},{"t":"coordination,"},{"t":"platforms and"},{"t":"knowledge exchange"},{"t":"To strengthen coordination, collaboration and knowledge exchange across actors and systems"},{"t":"• Strengthen national and regional platforms for education on biodiversity"},{"t":"Voluntary platforms or coordination mechanisms, shared repositories and knowledge exchange events"},{"t":"Parties, the Secretariat of the Convention, indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth organizations and other relevant organizations"},{"t":"Illustrative policy guidance, curriculum references and examples of alignment with global initiatives"},{"t":"Parties, educational authorities, indigenous peoples and local communities, and women’s and youth organizations"},{"t":"• Facilitate the exchange of resources, knowledge and experiences"},{"t":"• Support coordination among relevant actors and initiatives"},{"t":"Embedding education"},{"t":"in policy and"},{"t":"curriculum"},{"t":"frameworks"},{"t":"To embed education on"},{"t":"biodiversity, including on the state and trends of"},{"t":"biodiversity and the impacts and dependence of economic activities and societies on biodiversity, within policy, planning and curriculum"},{"t":"frameworks"},{"t":"• Integrate biodiversity into education policies, curricula and standards • Promote coherence between education and biodiversity-related policies and strategies"},{"t":"• Align education with national biodiversity priorities and whole-ofgovernment approaches"},{"t":"9/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 優先領域 | 目標 | 指示性行動 | 可能的成果物 | 指示性行為者 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|  | 加強生物多樣性教育在治理、標準與品質保證架構中的制度化整合 | • 將生物多樣性整合至教師職能標準與認證程序中 | 說明性職能架構、課程審查參考資料，以及制度性自我評估工具與指南 | 締約方、教育主管機關、認證機構、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織 |\n| | | • 使生物多樣性教育之目標與課程審查週期及評估架構一致，包括國際學生能力評量（Programme for International Student Assessment）氣候素養評量 | | |\n| | | • 將生物多樣性教育納入制度性發展計畫中 | | |\n| | | • 加強關於生物多樣性保育與永續利用的專業培訓 | | |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">優先領域</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">可能的成果物</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行為者</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">加強生物多樣性教育在治理、標準與品質保證架構中的制度化整合</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 將生物多樣性整合至教師職能標準與認證程序中</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">說明性職能架構、課程審查參考資料，以及制度性自我評估工具與指南</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、教育主管機關、認證機構、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 使生物多樣性教育之目標與課程審查週期及評估架構一致，包括國際學生能力評量（Programme for International Student Assessment）氣候素養評量</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 將生物多樣性教育納入制度性發展計畫中</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 加強關於生物多樣性保育與永續利用的專業培訓</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]},{"md":"**表 3**\n**預期成果 3：優先領域、目標、指示性行動、可能的成果物與指示性行為者**","html":"<p><strong>表 3</strong><br />\n<strong>預期成果 3：優先領域、目標、指示性行動、可能的成果物與指示性行為者</strong></p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]},{"md":"| 優先領域 | 目標 | 指示性行動 | 可能的成果物 | 指示性行為者 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 強化協調、平台與知識交流 | 加強不同行為者與系統間的協調、合作與知識交流 | • 強化生物多樣性教育之國家與區域平台 | 自願性平台或協調機制、共享資料庫與知識交流活動 | 締約方、公約秘書處、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關組織 |\n| | | • 促進資源、知識與經驗的交流<br>• 支持相關行為者與倡議之間的協調 | 說明性政策指南、課程參考資料以及與全球倡議一致之範例 | 締約方、教育主管機關、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織 |\n| 將教育嵌入政策與課程架構中 | 將生物多樣性教育（包括關於生物多樣性現況與趨勢，以及經濟活動與社會對生物多樣性的影響與依賴程度）嵌入政策、規劃與課程架構中 | • 將生物多樣性整合至教育政策、課程與標準中<br>• 促進教育與生物多樣性相關政策及策略之間的一致性<br>• 使教育與國家生物多樣性優先事項及全政府方法（whole-of-government approaches）一致 | | |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">優先領域</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">可能的成果物</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行為者</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">強化協調、平台與知識交流</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">加強不同行為者與系統間的協調、合作與知識交流</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 強化生物多樣性教育之國家與區域平台</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">自願性平台或協調機制、共享資料庫與知識交流活動</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、公約秘書處、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關組織</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 促進資源、知識與經驗的交流<br>• 支持相關行為者與倡議之間的協調</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">說明性政策指南、課程參考資料以及與全球倡議一致之範例</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、教育主管機關、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">將教育嵌入政策與課程架構中</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">將生物多樣性教育（包括關於生物多樣性現況與趨勢，以及經濟活動與社會對生物多樣性的影響與依賴程度）嵌入政策、規劃與課程架構中</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 將生物多樣性整合至教育政策、課程與標準中<br>• 促進教育與生物多樣性相關政策及策略之間的一致性<br>• 使教育與國家生物多樣性優先事項及全政府方法（whole-of-government approaches）一致</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[28,29,30,31,32]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p010.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Table 4"},{"t":"Cross-cutting enabling conditions: objectives, indicative actions, possible deliverables and indicative actors Cross-cutting enabling condition"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"Lifelong, life-wide and life-deep learning"},{"t":"To promote"},{"t":"continuous lifelong"},{"t":"learning across"},{"t":"formal, non-formal"},{"t":"and informal contexts"},{"t":"• Support learning across early childhood, youth, adult and professional education"},{"t":"Age-appropriate learning outcomes, awareness"},{"t":"initiatives and voluntary learning pathways"},{"t":"Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth"},{"t":"organizations, civil society and education providers, public institutions and private companies"},{"t":"Partnership initiatives, and outreach and awareness programmes"},{"t":"Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth"},{"t":"organizations, the private sector, civil society and public institutions"},{"t":"• Promote intergenerational and community-based learning • Strengthen continuity across learning pathways"},{"t":"• Support youth leadership platforms, intergenerational partnerships and mechanisms for youth participation in biodiversity-related decisionmaking and implementation processes"},{"t":"• Enhance access to and sustainable interaction with nature"},{"t":"Whole-of-society engagement"},{"t":"To foster inclusive"},{"t":"engagement across"},{"t":"sectors and"},{"t":"stakeholders"},{"t":"• Engage indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth, families, media and the private sector"},{"t":"• Strengthen partnerships and collaboration"},{"t":"• Support public engagement and cross-sector participation"},{"t":"10/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"表 4\n跨領域使能條件：目標、指標性行動、可能之成果與指標性行為者","html":"<p>表 4<br />\n跨領域使能條件：目標、指標性行動、可能之成果與指標性行為者</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"| 跨領域使能條件 | 目標 | 指標性行動 | 可能之成果 | 指標性行為者 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 終身、全方位且深層的學習 | 促進在正式、非正式及非正規情境下的持續終身學習 | • 支持涵蓋幼兒、青年、成人及專業教育的學習<br>• 促進跨世代與以社區為基礎的學習<br>• 強化學習路徑的連續性<br>• 支持青年領導平台、跨世代夥伴關係，以及青年參與生物多樣性相關決策與執行程序的機制<br>• 增進與自然之接觸及永續互動 | 符合年齡層之學習成果、覺察倡議與自願性學習路徑 | 締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、公民社會與教育提供者、公共機構與私營企業 |\n| 全社會參與 | 促進跨部門與利害關係人的包容性參與 | • 讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、家庭、媒體及私營部門參與<br>• 強化夥伴關係與協作<br>• 支持大眾參與及跨部門參與 | 夥伴關係倡議，以及推廣與覺察計畫 | 締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、私營部門、公民社會與公共機構 |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">跨領域使能條件</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指標性行動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">可能之成果</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指標性行為者</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">終身、全方位且深層的學習</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">促進在正式、非正式及非正規情境下的持續終身學習</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 支持涵蓋幼兒、青年、成人及專業教育的學習<br>• 促進跨世代與以社區為基礎的學習<br>• 強化學習路徑的連續性<br>• 支持青年領導平台、跨世代夥伴關係，以及青年參與生物多樣性相關決策與執行程序的機制<br>• 增進與自然之接觸及永續互動</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">符合年齡層之學習成果、覺察倡議與自願性學習路徑</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、公民社會與教育提供者、公共機構與私營企業</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">全社會參與</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">促進跨部門與利害關係人的包容性參與</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年、家庭、媒體及私營部門參與<br>• 強化夥伴關係與協作<br>• 支持大眾參與及跨部門參與</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">夥伴關係倡議，以及推廣與覺察計畫</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織、私營部門、公民社會與公共機構</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p011.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"Cross-cutting enabling condition"},{"t":"Objective"},{"t":"Indicative actions"},{"t":"Possible deliverables"},{"t":"Indicative actors"},{"t":"Sustainable financing and incentives"},{"t":"To support"},{"t":"sustainable,"},{"t":"accessible and"},{"t":"predictable financing"},{"t":"for education on"},{"t":"biodiversity"},{"t":"• Promote integration of education on biodiversity, including on the state and trends of biodiversity and the impacts and dependence of economic activities and societies on biodiversity, into national financing and budgeting processes"},{"t":"Illustrative financing"},{"t":"approaches, resource"},{"t":"mobilization examples and public-private partnerships"},{"t":"Parties, donors, indigenous peoples and local"},{"t":"communities, and women’s and youth organizations"},{"t":"• Support equitable and direct access to grant and research funding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth"},{"t":"• Allocate public funding to public academic establishments for biodiversity-related education programmes, curricula and awareness campaigns"},{"t":"• Encourage donors and financial mechanisms to ensure that financing for education on biodiversity is predictable, accessible and responsive to the specific circumstances of least developed countries and small island developing States"},{"t":"11/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6\n跨領域促成條件","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6<br />\n跨領域促成條件</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"| 目標 | 指示性行動 | 可能的成果物 | 指示性行為者 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **永續財務與誘因** | | | |\n| 支援生物多樣性教育之永續、可取得且可預測的財務 | • 促進將生物多樣性教育納入國家財務與預算程序，包括生物多樣性的現況與趨勢，以及經濟活動與社會對生物多樣性的影響與依賴 | 說明性財務方法、資源動員案例以及公私夥伴關係 | 締約方、捐助者、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織 |\n| | • 支援原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年公平且直接地取得補助與研究經費<br>• 向公立學術機構分配公共資金，用於生物多樣性相關之教育計畫、課程與宣導活動<br>• 鼓勵捐助者與財務機制確保生物多樣性教育之財務具備可預測性、可取得性，並能因應低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的特定情況 | | |","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">目標</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行動</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">可能的成果物</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">指示性行為者</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>永續財務與誘因</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">支援生物多樣性教育之永續、可取得且可預測的財務</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 促進將生物多樣性教育納入國家財務與預算程序，包括生物多樣性的現況與趨勢，以及經濟活動與社會對生物多樣性的影響與依賴</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">說明性財務方法、資源動員案例以及公私夥伴關係</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">締約方、捐助者、原住民族與地方社區，以及女性與青年組織</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">• 支援原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年公平且直接地取得補助與研究經費<br>• 向公立學術機構分配公共資金，用於生物多樣性相關之教育計畫、課程與宣導活動<br>• 鼓勵捐助者與財務機制確保生物多樣性教育之財務具備可預測性、可取得性，並能因應低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的特定情況</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","en":[17,18,19,20,21]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad70db349375d6d80094247/p012.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6"},{"t":"VI. Monitoring, evaluation and reporting"},{"t":"20. Monitoring, evaluation and reporting can be strengthened at the international level by inviting Parties to provide information on activities and policies involving the implementation of the global plan in their national communications, where possible, and in reports, including national reports, and by inviting indigenous peoples and local communities to submit information through their own reporting processes, including the Local Biodiversity Outlook and community-based monitoring and information systems. Such information could cover accomplishments, lessons learned, experience, challenges and opportunities and be used to develop indicators and monitoring mechanisms. Wherever possible, the information should be disaggregated by age and gender. For indigenous peoples and local communities, where appropriate, sex-disaggregated data and information on the participation, leadership and reach of indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth among them, could be systematically collected and used. The priority areas for action, objectives and indicative actions provide a useful guide for that purpose."},{"t":"21. In addition, entities of the United Nations system, other intergovernmental organizations and other non-Party stakeholders could be invited to submit information to the Secretariat on the implementation of the global plan at all levels."},{"t":"22. At the national level, Parties are encouraged to share with the public and all stakeholders the findings contained in their national communications and national biodiversity strategies and action plans or domestic programmes on biodiversity regarding the implementation of the global plan, using such tools as social media to reach and engage multiple stakeholders, as appropriate. Parties are also encouraged to involve indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and other stakeholders more closely in monitoring, evaluating and reporting on activities carried out under the global plan. Parties are further encouraged to report on the extent to which their activities with regard to education on biodiversity reflect transformative approaches and the meaningful participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth in the design and delivery of such activities."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"12/12"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.6</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"VI. 監測、評估與報告","html":"<p>VI. 監測、評估與報告</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"20. 透過邀請締約方在可能的情況下，於其國家通報中提供涉及執行全球計畫之活動與政策的資訊，並於報告（包括國家報告）中提供資訊，以及邀請原住民族與地方社區透過其自身的報告流程（包括地方生物多樣性展望以及以社區為基礎的監測與資訊系統）提交資訊，可以強化國際層級的監測、評估與報告。此類資訊可涵蓋成就、經驗教訓、經驗、挑戰與機會，並可用於開發指標與監測機制。在可能的情況下，資訊應按年齡與性別進行分類。針對原住民族與地方社區，在適當情況下，可系統性地收集並使用性別分類資料，以及關於原住民族與地方社區（包括其中的女性與青年）之參與、領導地位與影響範圍的資訊。行動的優先領域、目標與指示性行動為此目的提供了有用的指引。","html":"<p>20. 透過邀請締約方在可能的情況下，於其國家通報中提供涉及執行全球計畫之活動與政策的資訊，並於報告（包括國家報告）中提供資訊，以及邀請原住民族與地方社區透過其自身的報告流程（包括地方生物多樣性展望以及以社區為基礎的監測與資訊系統）提交資訊，可以強化國際層級的監測、評估與報告。此類資訊可涵蓋成就、經驗教訓、經驗、挑戰與機會，並可用於開發指標與監測機制。在可能的情況下，資訊應按年齡與性別進行分類。針對原住民族與地方社區，在適當情況下，可系統性地收集並使用性別分類資料，以及關於原住民族與地方社區（包括其中的女性與青年）之參與、領導地位與影響範圍的資訊。行動的優先領域、目標與指示性行動為此目的提供了有用的指引。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"21. 此外，可邀請聯合國系統之實體、其他政府間組織以及其他非締約方利害關係人，向秘書處提交各層級執行全球計畫之資訊。","html":"<p>21. 此外，可邀請聯合國系統之實體、其他政府間組織以及其他非締約方利害關係人，向秘書處提交各層級執行全球計畫之資訊。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"22. 在國家層級，鼓勵締約方與大眾及所有利害關係人分享其國家通報、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫或國內生物多樣性計畫中，關於執行全球計畫之研究結果，並在適當情況下，使用社群媒體等工具以接觸並參與多元利害關係人。亦鼓勵締約方更緊密地讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人參與全球計畫下所開展活動之監測、評估與報告。進一步鼓勵締約方報告其生物多樣性教育相關活動在多大程度上反映了轉型方法，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年在該等活動之設計與執行中的實質參與。","html":"<p>22. 在國家層級，鼓勵締約方與大眾及所有利害關係人分享其國家通報、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫或國內生物多樣性計畫中，關於執行全球計畫之研究結果，並在適當情況下，使用社群媒體等工具以接觸並參與多元利害關係人。亦鼓勵締約方更緊密地讓原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人參與全球計畫下所開展活動之監測、評估與報告。進一步鼓勵締約方報告其生物多樣性教育相關活動在多大程度上反映了轉型方法，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年在該等活動之設計與執行中的實質參與。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"__________","html":"<hr />","en":[4]},{"md":"12/12","html":"<p>12/12</p>","en":[5,6]}]}]};
